  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Counting an affirmation",
   "texto": [
    "**-다고 하다** is used to count an affirmation. La forma cambia según la palabra: adjetivo (피곤하다 → **피곤하다고**), verbo en presente (가다 → **간다고**, 먹다 → **먹는다고**) y sustantivo (학생이다 → **학생이라고**). En verbos que acaban en ㄹ, se pierde ㄹ antes de ㄴ: 살다 → **산다고**.",
    "민수 씨가 **피곤하다고** 했어요 = Minsu dijo que está cansado."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Past",
   "texto": [
    "The indirect past is formed with **-았다고 / -었다고**: PK (which was), PK (which slept), PK (which did).",
    "What he said is put in past with **했어요** (he said)."
   ]
